  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b7c55f32-42a2-4b6f-b7e6-a1f738bd94cf-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 184px;\" /><br /><br />Transformation axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are parallel. If&nbsp;the transformation&nbsp;axis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is making angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, it will make angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Therefore,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>&#952;cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
